# Milestone: M3
# Covers: when all strands are on the sleep queue (none on the ready queue),
#         sched_quiescent returns false (wakeup_pending_count > 0); after the
#         timer fires and strands are moved back to ready, quiescent stays false
#         until they finish, then becomes true.
#
# blocked: pending SCHED-13 vm_liveness QUIESCENT formalization (activate-or-fold decision)
# matrix-row: scheduler-quiescent
#
# UPDATE (v1.0 / M10): the lone-sleeper WAKE is now fixed (design-risks
# v0.11.4-A) — sched_wake_due_sleepers runs as a pre-dispatch pump in urbi_step,
# so an expired sleeper resumes (see the now-active wait_sleep_basic.chk and
# temporal/sleep_tag_stop.chk).
#
# UPDATE (v0.13.3, refactor-3 SCHED-01/B10): the original blocker — "a WAITING
# strand is intentionally counted in strand_runnable_count, so urbi_step
# returns RUNNING while any strand is parked" — is GONE.  Under the
# single-writer runnable count, WAITING strands are not counted: urbi_step now
# reports WAKE_AT while a sleeper is parked and QUIESCENT after it completes,
# and both edges are already asserted end-to-end by wait_sleep_basic.chk
# (QUIESCENT after completion) and temporal/sleep_tag_stop.chk (WAKE_AT while
# parked).  This fixture stays a placeholder pending the QUIESCENT-semantics
# formalization (vm_liveness, SCHED-13) in the same v0.13.3 arc tag, which
# owns the decision on whether to activate it or fold it into the two fixtures
# above.  The quiescence counter semantics themselves are unit-tested directly
# via the scheduler API (test_step_driver.c, test_scheduler_invariant.c).
